Task: Fix Windows CEF Clippy failures exposed after removing broad dead-code allowances.

Root cause:
- Unix-only constants and helpers were still compiled on Windows.
- Several test helpers were compiled for every test target although their callers exist only in Unix tests.
- WindowsOllamaDurableFs::cancel had no caller and was dead code.

Change:
- Gate platform-specific constants and helper methods at their real platform/test boundaries.
- Remove the unused Windows cancellation method.
- Keep the shared test helpers available on the targets that execute them.

Validation:
- cargo fmt --all -- --check: pass
- cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings: pass
- node ../scripts/ci/run-rust-test-filter.mjs --filter services::ollama_manager: 346 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored
- git diff --check: pass
- graphify update .: pass
- Local Windows cross-Clippy could not reach Beaver because aws-lc-sys requires Windows SDK headers unavailable on macOS; GitHub Windows CI is the authoritative platform validation.
